On Sep 5, 8:44 pm, Anvar Suyundikov <anvar.suyundi...@gmail.com>
wrote:

> I am plotting googlemaps using ggplot2 in R. I have recently met a
> problem with overlaying lines on the map.

You seem to be using geom_tile. Tiles often render with very thin
white lines between despite using size=0 or color=NA. There're some
workarounds, but better yet -- don't use geom_tile! Put the image as a
background for the plot. See [1] for some old info. These days it's
probably sufficient to do

library(png)
ggplot(...)
+ ...
+ scale_x_continuous(limits=c(xmin, xmax), expand=c(0, 0))
+ scale_y_continuous(limits=c(ymin, ymax), expand=c(0, 0))
+ opts(panel.background=(function () rasterGrob(readPNG(fname))))

[1] http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/browse_thread/thread/beff7d92f05dc741

