Hi

I think the problem I mentioned below (geom bar does not accept data
with NA) comes from the fact that ggplot calls pmin() without the
na.rm=TRUE argument.

  Indeed, if I change it in geom-bar.r
ymin = pmin(y, 0), ymax = pmax(y, 0),

to
ymin = pmin(y, 0, na.rm=TRUE), ymax = pmax(y, 0, na.rm=TRUE),

and recompile, I can run without problem:

df_withNA<-data.frame(value=c(runif(19),NA), factor=sample(c("A","B"),
size=20, replace=TRUE))
df_NoNA<-data.frame(value=runif(20), factor=sample(c("A","B"), size=20,
replace=TRUE))

qplot(x=factor, y=value, data=df_NoNA, geom="bar", stat="identity")
qplot(x=factor, y=value, data=df_withNA, geom="bar", stat="identity")

Do you confirm?

Thanks!!

Matthieu

